{"orgCode":"5196","name":"2011 State-Local Realignment","agencyCode":"4000","agencyName":"Health and Human Services","description":"Building upon the 1991-92 Realignment, 2011 Realignment moves program and fiscal responsibility to counties, providing a dedicated source of funding while eliminating duplication of effort, generating savings, and increasing flexibility.\n\nRealigned programs include local public safety programs, mental health, substance abuse, foster care, child welfare services, and adult protective services. Many of these programs are already administered at the local level by counties. Therefore, it is appropriate for the programmatic and fiscal responsibility to reside with the counties with the state maintaining an oversight and technical assistance role where needed. These changes are made with the goal of providing services more efficiently and at less cost.\n\nThe funding sources for realignment are:\n\n• The dedication of 1.0625 cents of a state special fund sales tax.\n\n• The dedication of a portion of vehicle license fee revenues.\n\nCounties receive 2011 Realignment funding from the following accounts and their related growth accounts:\n\n• Protective Services Subaccount (Foster Care, Child Welfare Services, and Adult Protective Services)\n\n• Behavioral Health Subaccount (Early and Periodic Screening, Diagnosis, and Treatment; Mental Health Managed Care; Substance Abuse Treatment; and Women and Children's Residential Treatment)\n\n• Mental Health Account (Community Mental Health Programs)\n\n• Trial Court Security Subaccount\n\n• Enhancing Law Enforcement Activities Subaccount (Local Jurisdiction for Lower-level Offenders and Parole Violators and Adult Parole)\n\n• Community Corrections Subaccount\n\n• District Attorney and Public Defender Subaccount\n\n• Juvenile Justice Subaccount (consisting of the Youthful Offender Block Grant Special Account and Juvenile Reentry Grant Special Account)\n\nThe funding reflected below and in the associated special display titled \"2011 Realignment Estimate\" is an estimate based on statutory formulas and the most recent Department of Finance revenue figures.","totals":{"amounts":{"py":6452303,"cy":6643985,"by":6787893},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0}},"programs":{"id":"exp/4000/5196","kind":"department","name":"2011 State-Local Realignment","code":"5196","amounts":{"py":6452303,"cy":6643985,"by":6787893},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":42758,"cy":49130,"by":59954},"special":{"py":6409545,"cy":6594855,"by":6727939}},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/5196/4360","kind":"program","name":"State-Local Realignment, 2011","code":"4360","amounts":{"py":6452303,"cy":6643985,"by":6787893},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":42758,"cy":49130,"by":59954},"special":{"py":6409545,"cy":6594855,"by":6727939}},"positions":{"py":0,"cy":0,"by":0},"extra":{"byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":6452303,"cy":6643985,"by":6787893}},"apiProgramLine":true},"children":[{"id":"exp/4000/5196/4360/f0001","kind":"fund","name":"General Fund","code":"0001","amounts":{"py":42758,"cy":49130,"by":59954},"byFundType":{"general":{"py":42758,"cy":49130,"by":59954}},"extra":{"fundType":"general","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":42758,"cy":49130,"by":59954}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/5196/4360/f0351","kind":"fund","name":"Mental Health Subaccount, Sales Tax Account","code":"0351","amounts":{"py":1122442,"cy":1130230,"by":1128230},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":1122442,"cy":1130230,"by":1128230}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":1122442,"cy":1130230,"by":1128230}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/5196/4360/f3171","kind":"fund","name":"Local Revenue Fund 2011","code":"3171","amounts":{"py":-42758,"cy":-49130,"by":-59953},"byFundType":{"special":{"py":-42758,"cy":-49130,"by":-59953}},"extra":{"fundType":"special","byAppropriationType":{"Local Assistance":{"py":-42758,"cy":-49130,"by":-59953}}}},{"id":"exp/4000/5196/4360/f3216","kind":"fun